# Open Knowledge Format (OKF)

Repo-root bundle (Option A). Spec: https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog/blob/main/okf/SPEC.md

## Knowledge vs docs (mandatory)

| Folder | Purpose | Companion |
|---|---|---|
| `knowledge/` | **General knowledge** — portable reference, design patterns, not project-specific contracts | `knowledge/README.md` |
| `docs/` | **This project's implementation** — how the project is built and behaves (architecture, invariants, local runtime, verification) | `docs/README.md` |

Agents: read the companion README before choosing where to write. Project truth and runbooks → `docs/` (or owning service README). General patterns → `knowledge/` (human-owned; agent frontmatter only on existing files).

## Folder ownership (mandatory)

| Path | Who creates files | Agent may write | OKF indexed |
|---|---|---|---|
| `knowledge/` | **Human only** | **Frontmatter only** on existing files — no new files, no body edits, no renames/deletes | Yes — `knowledge/index.md` |
| `docs/` | **Human or agent** | Full create, edit, rename (with index sync) | Yes — `docs/index.md` |
| `api/README.md`, `frontend/README.md` | **Human or agent** | Full edit per `documentation-diagrams.mdc` | **No** — not part of OKF bundle |

**Agent forbidden in `knowledge/`:** create a new `.md`, delete or rename a concept, edit prose/body below frontmatter, add index bullets for files the human did not create. If project truth or a runbook is needed, write under `docs/` (or the owning service README), not `knowledge/`.

**When human adds a `knowledge/` file:** agent may add or refresh OKF frontmatter (`type`, `title`, `description`, `tags`, `timestamp`) and ask the human to update `knowledge/index.md`, or update `index.md` only when syncing an existing human-added file.

SOP: `.cursor/skills/how-to-okf/SKILL.md`.

## Full map (mandatory for OKF folders)

Every concept under `knowledge/` and `docs/` **must** have OKF YAML frontmatter (`type`, `title`, `description`, `tags`).

- **Coverage:** all `*.md` in those folders except `index.md`, `knowledge/README.md`, and `docs/README.md` (folder companions).
- **Indexes:** `knowledge/index.md` and `docs/index.md` list every concept in that folder.
- **Check:** `python3 scripts/okf-check.py` when adding, renaming, or removing `docs/` concepts (or after human adds `knowledge/` files + frontmatter).
- **Rehydrate:** `python3 scripts/okf-rehydrate-index.py` after frontmatter or `docs/` edits.

## Navigation (read path)

- **Entry:** [/index.md](/index.md) — do not preload the whole tree.
- **General reference (read-only concepts):** [/knowledge/index.md](/knowledge/index.md)
- **Project contracts / runbooks (agent-writable):** [/docs/index.md](/docs/index.md)
- **Service specifics:** `api/README.md`, `frontend/README.md` — direct open when editing; **not** in OKF index.
- **Harness:** `.cursor/rules/` — not OKF. Router: `AGENTS.md`.

Scan frontmatter `description` / `tags` / optional `disclosure` (`router` | `on_demand` | `background`) before opening full concept bodies.

## Write path — `docs/` only (agent)

New or substantially edited `.md` under `docs/` (except `index.md`):

1. YAML frontmatter with `type`, `title`, `description`, `tags`, `timestamp`.
2. Bundle-relative links: `/knowledge/...`, `/docs/...`.
3. Update `docs/index.md` bullet.
4. Run `python3 scripts/okf-rehydrate-index.py` and `python3 scripts/okf-check.py` before handback.

## Write path — `knowledge/` (agent: frontmatter only)

On an **existing** human-owned file only:

1. Add or update the YAML frontmatter block.
2. Do **not** change body content unless the user explicitly asks for a human-co-authored edit.

Do **not** create `log.md` — git history is the changelog.

## Exempt from OKF

- `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, `.cursor/hooks/`
- `knowledge/README.md`, `docs/README.md` — folder companions (not OKF concepts)
- **`api/README.md`, `frontend/README.md`** — service container docs; `documentation-diagrams.mdc` applies, not OKF

## Handback

List **knowledge:** or **docs:** paths in reply attribution when read or written. Run `okf-check.py` when `docs/` concepts changed.
